  "segments": [
    {
      "v": "narrator",
      "t": "Disaster strikes when the thrown coconut hits the Michelin inspector instead of Senya. When the terrified inspector wakes up, Chef Barinov desperately tries to calm him down and asks Fedya to escort him to his room.",
      "gap": 0.8
    },
    {
      "v": "fedya",
      "t": "Шеф, это были просто кокосы.",
      "gap": 0.55
    },
    {
      "v": "anya",
      "t": "Замолчи сейчас же, Федя!",
      "gap": 0.55
    },
    {
      "v": "fedya",
      "t": "Сейчас приведу его в чувство.",
      "gap": 0.55
    },
    {
      "v": "anya",
      "t": "Стойте на месте!",
      "gap": 0.55
    },
    {
      "v": "fedya",
      "t": "Шеф, извините меня, пожалуйста.",
      "gap": 0.55
    },
    {
      "v": "inspector",
      "t": "Пожалуйста, не убивайте меня.",
      "gap": 0.55
    },
    {
      "v": "anya",
      "t": "Мы не желаем вам зла.",
      "gap": 0.55
    },
    {
      "v": "inspector",
      "t": "А зачем вы меня ударили?",
      "gap": 0.55
    },
    {
      "v": "anya",
      "t": "Это просто глупое недоразумение.",
      "gap": 0.55
    },
    {
      "v": "inspector",
      "t": "Отпустите меня отсюда, пожалуйста.",
      "gap": 0.55
    },
    {
      "v": "anya",
      "t": "Конечно, вы совершенно свободны.",
      "gap": 0.55
    },
    {
      "v": "anya",
      "t": "Хотите пойти к себе в номер?",
      "gap": 0.55
    },
    {
      "v": "anya",
      "t": "Федя, проводи человека, пожалуйста.",
      "gap": 0.9
    },
    {
      "v": "narrator",
      "t": "Now let's go back through their conversation line by line and unpack the Russian phrasing.",
      "gap": 0.4
    },
    {
      "v": "fedya",
      "t": "Шеф, это были просто кокосы.",
      "gap": 0.55
    },
    {
      "v": "narrator",
      "t": "'Chef, those were just coconuts.' Spoken Russian keeps this brisk, leaning on 'Chef Barinov' and finishing on 'coconuts'. Chef Barinov answers right away.",
      "gap": 0.4
    },
    {
      "v": "anya",
      "t": "Замолчи сейчас же, Федя!",
      "gap": 0.55
    },
    {
      "v": "narrator",
      "t": "'Be quiet right now, Fedya!' Chef Barinov anchors the line on 'shut up', while 'Fedya' completes the thought.",
      "gap": 0.4
    },
    {
      "v": "fedya",
      "t": "Сейчас приведу его в чувство.",
      "gap": 0.55
    },
    {
      "v": "narrator",
      "t": "'I will bring him to his senses now.' Spoken Russian keeps this brisk, leaning on 'now' and finishing on 'feeling'.",
      "gap": 0.4
    },
    {
      "v": "anya",
      "t": "Стойте на месте!",
      "gap": 0.55
    },
    {
      "v": "narrator",
      "t": "'Stand right there!' Notice how Russian expresses 'stop' and 'place' with crisp inflection rather than helper words. Fedya answers right away.",
      "gap": 0.4
    },
    {
      "v": "fedya",
      "t": "Шеф, извините меня, пожалуйста.",
      "gap": 0.55
    },
    {
      "v": "narrator",
      "t": "'Chef, excuse me, please.' Here the Russian phrasing highlights 'Chef Barinov' before landing on 'please'.",
      "gap": 0.4
    },
    {
      "v": "inspector",
      "t": "Пожалуйста, не убивайте меня.",
      "gap": 0.55
    },
    {
      "v": "narrator",
      "t": "'Please do not kill me.' The meaning hinges on 'please' working together with 'me' in spoken Russian.",
      "gap": 0.4
    },
    {
      "v": "anya",
      "t": "Мы не желаем вам зла.",
      "gap": 0.55
    },
    {
      "v": "narrator",
      "t": "'We do not wish you any harm.' Chef Barinov chooses the respectful plural 'you' alongside 'evil' to keep a polite distance. the inspector answers right away.",
      "gap": 0.4
    },
    {
      "v": "inspector",
      "t": "А зачем вы меня ударили?",
      "gap": 0.55
    },
    {
      "v": "narrator",
      "t": "'Then why did you hit me?' The grammar packs 'and' and 'to hit' into a tight, idiomatic kitchen exchange.",
      "gap": 0.4
    },
    {
      "v": "anya",
      "t": "Это просто глупое недоразумение.",
      "gap": 0.55
    },
    {
      "v": "narrator",
      "t": "'This is just a foolish misunderstanding.' The meaning hinges on 'this' working together with 'misunderstanding' in spoken Russian.",
      "gap": 0.4
    },
    {
      "v": "inspector",
      "t": "Отпустите меня отсюда, пожалуйста.",
      "gap": 0.55
    },
    {
      "v": "narrator",
      "t": "'Let me go from here, please.' In Russian, the idea of 'let go' flows naturally into 'please' without extra filler words. Chef Barinov answers right away.",
      "gap": 0.4
    },
    {
      "v": "anya",
      "t": "Конечно, вы совершенно свободны.",
      "gap": 0.55
    },
    {
      "v": "narrator",
      "t": "'Of course, you are completely free.' Chef Barinov anchors the line on 'of course', while 'free' completes the thought.",
      "gap": 0.4
    },
    {
      "v": "anya",
      "t": "Хотите пойти к себе в номер?",
      "gap": 0.55
    },
    {
      "v": "narrator",
      "t": "'Do you want to go to your room?' The grammar packs 'want' and 'number' into a tight, idiomatic kitchen exchange.",
      "gap": 0.4
    },
    {
      "v": "anya",
      "t": "Федя, проводи человека, пожалуйста.",
      "gap": 0.55
    },
    {
      "v": "narrator",
      "t": "'Fedya, escort the man, please.' Here the Russian phrasing highlights 'Fedya' before landing on 'please'. Alright, let's hear the entire conversation one more time from start to finish.",
